    "created_at": "2018-02-06T23:04:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-06T23:05:16Z",
    "body": "My guess is that it would:\r\n* **resolve** when the message is successfully delivered (the event loop spins and the callbacks, if any, are run for the event; possibly it would just post a task before posting the actual message, so you don't have to wait for the message callback to finish, but are still pretty sure it got there and is about to run), \r\n* **reject** when the message is going to be dropped instead (frozen or discarded tab being messaged by a SW)\r\n* **stay pending** if the message still *might* be delivered, but hasn't done so yet (a window still spinning up, which doesn't have its message loop working *yet*, but which should have it working in a little bit and will deliver the pending messages then).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
